  "interpretation": "Zero-shot transfer fails, which E2 already established. What this run adds is the price of fixing it: the smallest labelled budget from the target network at which the detector becomes usable, and whether transferring from the source is worth anything at that budget compared with training on the target data alone. Where fine-tuning does not beat target-only training at the same budget, we say so, because that is the case in which the source model contributes nothing and an operator should not use it.",
